(82592, 3069, 1379, '<td valign="top">You really DID get close!  I love the amazing detail you caputured in this little fella''s body.  That mottled yellow/ black is really cool.  Great shot!</td>', 'You really DID get close!  I love the amazing detail you caputured in this little fella''s body.  That mottled yellow/ black is really cool.  Great shot!', '2002-07-14 18:27:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(82593, 3069, 2, '<td valign="top">Wow -- that is close.  I''m sure you''ve gotten this criticism already, but I don''t really like the wasted white space on the right of the image.</td>', 'Wow -- that is close.  I''m sure you''ve gotten this criticism already, but I don''t really like the wasted white space on the right of the image.', '2002-07-14 21:45:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(82594, 3069, 1078, '<td valign="top">Very sharp.  Nice DOF.  Appreciate that the shadows fromt he flash are mostly all hidden behind the nest.  I like the upside down composition and the minimal color.  If I had to find fault, it would be with the streak that, I assume, is on the wood behind the wasp -- it looks like it''s coming out of its tail?  I''d consider cloning that out in future versions -- but nothing you can do about it for this competition.</td>', 'Very sharp.  Nice DOF.  Appreciate that the shadows fromt he flash are mostly all hidden behind the nest.  I like the upside down composition and the minimal color.  If I had to find fault, it would be with the streak that, I assume, is on the wood behind the wasp -- it looks like it''s coming out of its tail?  I''d consider cloning that out in future versions -- but nothing you can do about it for this competition.', '2002-07-15 00:26:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(82595, 3069, 1202, '<td valign="top">Just a quick note to thank you all for the nice and interesting comments and votes.   My "That''s Close Enough" picture was fairly difficult for me as she would not pose.   I had been perched on a ladder long enough that I really wanted to reach out and turn her just a little.   When I did take a shot I would get her out of focus or she had the wrong end pointing at the lens.   I got one of her with her stinger ready for action, and then I took a little break so she might settle down.   I am real pleased with placing 14th, as I knew it was on the edge for a true "Fear" shot.<br/>Oh by the way. No she isn''t plastic, nor is she upside down, this is the way they hang.   I should have entered her the other way around because she is a lot more intimidating.<br/>Thanks, Autool<br/></td>', 'Just a quick note to thank you all for the nice and interesting comments and votes.   My "That''s Close Enough" picture was fairly difficult for me as she would not pose.   I had been perched on a ladder long enough that I really wanted to reach out and turn her just a little.   When I did take a shot I would get her out of focus or she had the wrong end pointing at the lens.   I got one of her with her stinger ready for action, and then I took a little break so she might settle down.   I am real pleased with placing 14th, as I knew it was on the edge for a true "Fear" shot.Oh by the way. No she isn''t plastic, nor is she upside down, this is the way they hang.   I should have entered her the other way around because she is a lot more intimidating.Thanks, Autool', '2002-07-15 22:02:00.000000', NULL, 0),
