(83007, 3087, 2221, '<td valign="top">ugh. very very reddish. somehoe this photo looks like one of these pictures in learning books for doctors. i would have done the following: in your photo editor desaturate all reddish tones and only leave the blue ones (blue, cyan). this would have the interesting effect of having the nice blue pupill without the strong red tones, ephasizing the eye more.</td>', 'ugh. very very reddish. somehoe this photo looks like one of these pictures in learning books for doctors. i would have done the following: in your photo editor desaturate all reddish tones and only leave the blue ones (blue, cyan). this would have the interesting effect of having the nice blue pupill without the strong red tones, ephasizing the eye more.', '2002-07-13 21:23:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(83008, 3087, 806, '<td valign="top">The iris/pupil and red around the eye is dramatic, but I don''t like the yellow-ish tinge to the skin. Detracts from the eye. I looked at this all week to try to understand how I feel about it... now Sat. night, and I still don''t have any useful comment, except that, and also the focus could be a bit sharper.</td>', 'The iris/pupil and red around the eye is dramatic, but I don''t like the yellow-ish tinge to the skin. Detracts from the eye. I looked at this all week to try to understand how I feel about it... now Sat. night, and I still don''t have any useful comment, except that, and also the focus could be a bit sharper.', '2002-07-14 00:20:00.000000', NULL, 1),
