(83372, 3102, 1078, '<td valign="top">Love the idea, have some problems with the set up.  I think I can understand why you''d use silk flowers for the shot, but in the context of the picture they seem really tacky.  Would you give/expect silk flowers from your lover in terms of getting engaged?  Second, the note looks typed out -- bad enough to turn someone down via a note, but to not even make it a handwritten one?  And then to keep the ring and just give back the box with the note inside?  If you''d used real flowers, left the ring in the box, and the placed the note off to one side in the composition, I''d have upped my score.  :-)</td>', 'Love the idea, have some problems with the set up.  I think I can understand why you''d use silk flowers for the shot, but in the context of the picture they seem really tacky.  Would you give/expect silk flowers from your lover in terms of getting engaged?  Second, the note looks typed out -- bad enough to turn someone down via a note, but to not even make it a handwritten one?  And then to keep the ring and just give back the box with the note inside?  If you''d used real flowers, left the ring in the box, and the placed the note off to one side in the composition, I''d have upped my score.  :-)', '2002-07-14 18:52:00.000000', NULL, 1),
